{"chunk_id": "0d42dc3415d9", "text": "These sections recount the rise of Skanda (Kartikeya) as a divine war leader. Surrounded by gods, sages, planets, and fierce Mother goddesses, the young deity attracts the attention of Indra, who marches against him with the celestial army. When the gods attack, Skanda releases flames from his mouth that devastate their forces. Indra strikes him with the thunderbolt, but from the wound another powerful youth, Visakha, is born, terrifying the gods and forcing Indra to seek Skanda\u2019s protection. The sages then urge Skanda to become ruler of the three worlds, yet he refuses Indra\u2019s throne and instead accepts the role of commander of the celestial hosts. Honored by the gods and blessed with divine virtues, Skanda is anointed as the general who will lead the gods against the Danavas.\nSkanda battles Indra, generates the warrior Visakha from the thunderbolt wound, then refuses Indra\u2019s throne and is anointed commander of the celestial armies.\nThemes: divine warfare, birth of Visakha, legitimization of Skanda, cosmic hierarchy, leadership and humility", "vector": [0.0017306685913354158, -0.019103411585092545, 0.0018809461034834385, 0.006278628017753363, -0.0056147645227611065, 0.01664612628519535, -0.04320066049695015, -0.017874768003821373, -0.011830639094114304, -0.01379250455647707, 0.013065887615084648, 0.0056147645227611065, -0.0013789201620966196, 0.0014565360033884645, -0.0068434071727097034, 0.014822978526353836, 0.040003545582294464, -0.019882872700691223, 0.003294545691460371, -0.009419593028724194, -0.013633969239890575, -0.004088869784027338, 0.0015308490255847573, 0.009188396856188774, -0.027056559920310974, 0.014043517410755157, 0.02520699054002762, -0.024150094017386436, 0.006830195896327496, -0.006219177506864071, -0.00418465118855238, -0.009181791916489601, 0.0064041344448924065, -0.0005924402503296733, -0.023317787796258926, -0.0005878988886252046, 0.010093364864587784, -0.03651578724384308, 8.2776496128